# C06 manage draft read — session binding closed

Issue: https://github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-remote-ops/issues/5
Repo: github.com/liboyang42-cpu/chengyin-ios
Branch: cursor/c06-manage-draft-read-e504
Base: cursor/c06-theme-draft-request-read-e504 @ eeac4a3d34bddec04f3132c10e981cc0db0e0c18

`MerchantOperationsEditor.readHeldThemeDraft` calls the existing
`MerchantNPCThemeDraftRequestRead`. It first calls `holdThemeDraftRequest`
with the member id and request id the original author request already produced.
It then calls `readAndRecover`. A missing held id returns before that call, so
it does not GET and does not publish. A missing publisher stays unpublished.
The editor does not POST `api/ai/theme/draft` and does not publish an approved
revision. It does not mint either id. The editor calls the reader. It does not discard the caller.

The nested manage page stays `MerchantStoreCharacterView` plus the manage
`NavigationLink` into `MerchantOperationsDocumentView`. This hunk does not
replace that page with an older character page and does not revert
`MerchantOperationsEditor` to a document-only page.

## Not applied

Passing the held request into the nested manage link needs the session binding.
That attach is only the paste below. Do not apply it. Do not edit:

```
App/AppSession.swift
App/AppCompositionRoot.swift
Questify.xcodeproj/project.pbxproj
```

Not inserted into `merchantOperationsDestination` or
`merchantStoreCharacterDestination`. `publisher` stays nil. Do not mint a
member id or a request id. If the original author request did not already
produce both, pass nil and the editor sends nothing.

```swift
if destination == .character,
   let merchantID = access.identity.merchantID,
   let row = PublicMerchantRowID(merchantID),
   let scope = merchantNPCScope(row: row),
   let api = regionalConfiguration?.apiConfiguration {
    let flow = MerchantNPCKnowledgeAuthorFlow(
        scope: scope,
        publisher: nil,
        currentScope: { [weak self] in self?.merchantNPCScope(row: row) })
    let caller = MerchantNPCThemeDraftRequestRead(
        configuration: api,
        transport: runtimeHTTPTransport,
        memberID: { [weak self] in self?.account.map { Int64($0.id) } },
        token: { [weak self] in self?.token })
    let heldMember = flow.heldThemeDraftMemberID
    let heldRequest = flow.heldThemeDraftRequestID
    return merchantStoreCharacterDestination(
        authorFlow: flow,
        themeDraftRequestRead: caller,
        draftReadMemberID: heldMember,
        draftReadRequestID: heldRequest)
}

func merchantStoreCharacterDestination(
    authorFlow: MerchantNPCKnowledgeAuthorFlow? = nil,
    themeDraftRequestRead: MerchantNPCThemeDraftRequestRead? = nil,
    draftReadMemberID: Int64? = nil,
    draftReadRequestID: String? = nil) -> AnyView {
    AnyView(SessionMerchantStoreCharacterView(
        reader: merchantOperationsReader,
        npcSaveReader: merchantNPCSaveOperationsReader,
        authorFlow: authorFlow,
        themeDraftRequestRead: themeDraftRequestRead,
        draftReadMemberID: draftReadMemberID,
        draftReadRequestID: draftReadRequestID))
}

NavigationLink {
    MerchantOperationsDocumentView(
        reader: npcSaveReader,
        destination: .character,
        authorFlow: authorFlow,
        draftReadMemberID: draftReadMemberID,
        draftReadRequestID: draftReadRequestID,
        themeDraftRequestRead: themeDraftRequestRead)
} label: { Text("manage", tableName: "MerchantNPCSaveReceipt") }
MerchantStoreCharacterView(coordinator: StoreCharacterCoordinator(reader: StoreCharacterOperationsReader(reader: reader)))
```

The paste passes `caller` into the existing nested manage destination. It does
not drop that value and does not call the read from the session. The manage
editor calls the read. Not inserted.

